From 0599b551c0895367599a248d395f17f9ba767cb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 14:53:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 514/572] feat(stm32mp2-fdts): Use a generic name for the PMIC
 node

The ePAPR standard says that: "the name of a node should be somewhat
generic, reflecting the function of the device and not its precise
programming model."

So, change the stpmic binding document to use a generic name
with pattern: "^pmic@[0-9]$" and update the associated device tree,
using a alias with the real PMIC model: STPMIC25.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 2ca8a6c87d1177c06fd3797b79b2574f9ddd677e feat(stm32mp2-fdts): Use a generic name for the PMIC node]
Signed-off-by: Patrick Delaunay <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
